 below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{-5}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}7-3x, & x<-1 \\\\ 10, & x\\ge -1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296647 1113 #uuid "bebd9b42-4c15-5a4c-bcc4-3722f4a7881d" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296647 1145 "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-5}^{-1}(7-3x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}10\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(7x-3\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}){|}_{-5}^{-1}+10x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =[7(-1)-3\\frac{(-1)^{2}}{2}-7(-5)+3\\frac{(-5)^{2}}{2}]+10[(1)-(-1)] \\\\  & =[28+36]+10[2] \\\\  & =64+20 \\\\  & =84.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296648 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296649 13194139534578 true] [17592186296648 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296650 13194139534578 true] [17592186296648 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296651 13194139534578 true] [17592186296648 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296652 13194139534578 true] [17592186296648 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296653 13194139534578 true] [17592186296648 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534578 true] [17592186296648 1041 "selection" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296648 1104 #edb/ref 17592186296652 13194139534578 true] [17592186296648 1110 #uuid "826651a7-01f6-5aa1-8623-1d556360809b" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296649 1034 "64" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296649 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534578 true] [17592186296649 1111 #uuid "2d5e053e-2fd0-5b0e-bf97-ca02452a3d11" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296650 1034 "62" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296650 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534578 true] [17592186296650 1111 #uuid "9ea249d8-30d5-5804-84dd-69702ba7be1c" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296651 1034 "21" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296651 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534578 true] [17592186296651 1111 #uuid "48686f43-375c-5027-b3aa-9095101538ac" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296652 1034 "84" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296652 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534578 true] [17592186296652 1111 #uuid "4a1ea743-cf10-507e-ac95-e3e545c984ed" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296653 1034 "42" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296653 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534578 true] [17592186296653 1111 #uuid "84d8ab6b-d244-5fb6-bd0d-7bd83a787197" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296654 1017 #edb/ref 17592186296655 13194139534578 true] [17592186296654 1089 "q-117669" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296654 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534578 true] [17592186296654 1100 "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}1-{x}^{2}, & x<0 \\\\ 2x+1, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296654 1113 #uuid "eaf2bfbd-fd1d-5fe9-ac11-0df52f6066be" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296654 1145 "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}){|}_{-2}^{0}+({x}^{2}+x){|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[(0)-\\frac{(0)^{3}}{3}-(-2)+\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3}]+[(2)^{2}+2-(0)^{2}-(0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}+6 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296655 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296656 13194139534578 true] [17592186296655 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296657 13194139534578 true] [17592186296655 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296658 13194139534578 true] [17592186296655 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296659 13194139534578 true] [17592186296655 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296660 13194139534578 true] [17592186296655 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534578 true] [17592186296655 1041 "selection" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296655 1104 #edb/ref 17592186296657 13194139534578 true] [17592186296655 1110 #uuid "eeef0fcf-c965-51e2-b18c-4f01c8f232f0" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296656 1034 "\\frac{20}{3}" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296656 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534578 true] [17592186296656 1111 #uuid "77aaf520-58b8-502a-8c99-aa6ccf2212ec" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296657 1034 "\\frac{16}{3}" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296657 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534578 true] [17592186296657 1111 #uuid "89e4c37f-f88c-57b1-9263-b4a9fb440858" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296658 1034 "\\frac{14}{3}" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296658 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534578 true] [17592186296658 1111 #uuid "661af475-d92a-5fa0-a02c-051a8ea83cce" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296659 1034 "6" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534578 true] [17592186296659 1111 #uuid "e921000f-4906-542d-85d7-1f44c483694a" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296660 1034 "4" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296660 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534578 true] [17592186296660 1111 #uuid "366bc398-d197-5005-85ec-47cddefb648e" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296661 1017 #edb/ref 17592186296662 13194139534578 true] [17592186296661 1089 "q-117702" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296661 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534578 true] [17592186296661 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036389/assets/f725b571954587b7b88426a254d7a6fc05f09b63ab2cc94b81303a510e8c1798.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of two line segments. Find the value of ${\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296661 1113 #uuid "5e1ef3f5-5fb9-5108-bf98-1048434bd777" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296661 1145 "We divide the interval of integration into $3$ regions: the line segment for $x\\in [-2,0],$ the line segment for $x\\in [0,2),$ and the line segment for $x\\in [2,3].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-2}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,0].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,2).$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [2,3].$ The corresponding region is a rectangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =bh \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2}+{A}_{3} \\\\  & =2-2+2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296663 13194139534578 true] [17592186296662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296664 13194139534578 true] [17592186296662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296665 13194139534578 true] [17592186296662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296666 13194139534578 true] [17592186296662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296667 13194139534578 true] [17592186296662 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534578 true] [17592186296662 1041 "selection" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296662 1104 #edb/ref 17592186296664 13194139534578 true] [17592186296662 1110 #uuid "656e0866-f42a-5d57-9e9d-258ff950f4fe" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296663 1034 "8" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296663 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534578 true] [17592186296663 1111 #uuid "682b381d-5e6e-5160-94ad-9d4a8ed756e6" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296664 1034 "2" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296664 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534578 true] [17592186296664 1111 #uuid "650bc56e-d4be-56f7-9782-82bca026b5e7" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296665 1034 "6" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296665 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534578 true] [17592186296665 1111 #uuid "1adc9afb-e7c0-5fdd-a4d3-c3dd940dc26b" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296666 1034 "1" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296666 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534578 true] [17592186296666 1111 #uuid "b683bc48-e786-553b-b5a2-9cff7eb61c5f" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296667 1034 "4" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296667 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534578 true] [17592186296667 1111 #uuid "abf7b063-ee50-5728-ad99-832cfe7442cc" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296668 1017 #edb/ref 17592186296669 13194139534578 true] [17592186296668 1089 "q-18004" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296668 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534578 true] [17592186296668 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036389/assets/d43fa0efcfb8788316c86958b1175741c136588e81a8119131d1ca0f8d8ee229.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of four line segments. Find the value of ${\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296668 1113 #uuid "a3e6f460-32b8-5013-a35b-ba52c5b54bbc" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296668 1145 "The graph consists of four parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-3,-2),$ the line segment for $x\\in [-2,-1),$ the line segment for $x\\in [-1,1),$ and the line segments for $x\\in [1,3].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{4}}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-3,-2).$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,-1).$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-1,1).$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $4$th integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,3].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{4}=-2.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2}+{A}_{3}-{A}_{4} \\\\  & =1-1+2-2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534578 true] [17592186296669 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296670 13194139534578 true] [17592186296669 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296671 13194139534578 true] [17592186296669 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296672 13194139534578 true] [17592186296669 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296673 13194139534578 true] [17592186296669 1000 #edb/ref 17592186296674 13194139534578 true] [17592186296669 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534578 true] [17592186296669 1041 "selection" 13194139534578 true] [1759218629666